# ---- Firebase Authentication (Google Sign-In) ----
# Get these values from Firebase Console → Your Project → Project Settings → Your apps → Web App (create one if needed, it's free).
# Step-by-step guide:
#   1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com/ and create a project (or open existing).
#   2. Add a "Web app" (click the </> icon). Copy the config object shown.
#   3. Firebase Console → Authentication → Sign-in method → enable "Google".
#   4. Firebase Console → Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains → add every domain where you will host this site
#      (for local dev: localhost; for production: yourdomain.com, also add your Vercel/Netlify preview domains e.g. *.vercel.app).
#   5. Paste the 6 values below. Leave them quoted or unquoted. They are built into the JS bundle (public by nature) — that's normal for Firebase Web SDK.
#   6. Restart `npm run dev` after editing this file.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
